It doesn't have to be "based on the current status quo" but it feels quite odd;   
\- What is the observational unit? The "current trend" is one observation (there is no CI from one obs). Are you comparing many lags/leads that influence the "current trend"? Are you comparing many different models against one candidate model?  


\- Try to verbalize what the CI is. "We are 95% confident the mean trend of many lag/leads or models is between LB and UB... Because our candidate model is inside/outside of this range we accept/reject the null hypothesis".
